  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Chemery</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Chemery (modern Ch\u00e9mery) was the site of an important Gallo-Roman productive center for sigillate pottery. It was, in fact, the principal pottery of Saturninus and Satto.",
